('127.33.d.1.A',2,'A student in an energy and natural resources class starts an SAE. Which describes planning it well?','["setting goals, a timeline and a way to measure results", "picking a project at random", "skipping the paperwork", "waiting until the last week"]'::jsonb,0,'Good SAE programs are planned, carried out and evaluated.','original'),
('127.33.d.1.A',2,'After finishing a wind-energy SAE project, the student should:','["throw away the records", "evaluate what worked and what to change", "ignore the results", "start over without review"]'::jsonb,1,'Evaluation is the last step of an SAE.','original'),
('127.33.d.1.B',2,'A student tracks hours worked on a conservation project. This is an example of:','["gossip", "advertising", "record keeping", "fundraising only"]'::jsonb,2,'Hours and expenses are SAE records.','original'),
('127.33.d.1.B',2,'Which record belongs in an SAE for a land management project?','["guesses", "rumors", "jokes", "dates, costs and income"]'::jsonb,3,'Accurate financial and time records are required.','original'),
('127.33.d.1.C',2,'Serving as a committee chair in an agricultural club gives a student:','["leadership experience", "fewer friends", "no skills", "less confidence"]'::jsonb,0,'Leadership roles build skills.','original'),
('127.33.d.1.C',2,'A well-rounded experience program includes:','["only watching videos", "work, learning and leadership activities", "no activity", "only sleeping"]'::jsonb,1,'Balanced programs build many skills.','original'),
('127.33.d.1.D',2,'A chapter''s yearly program of activities is built by:','["avoiding planning", "guessing", "setting goals and assigning tasks", "ignoring members"]'::jsonb,2,'Strategic planning organizes the program.','original'),
('127.33.d.1.D',2,'Participating in a local chapter program means:','["avoiding events", "skipping meetings", "hiding from teams", "taking part in planned events"]'::jsonb,3,'Participation completes the plan.','original'),
('127.33.d.2.A',2,'During a field investigation of soil, students should:','["follow safety rules and wear proper gear", "ignore hazards", "skip instructions", "run across the site"]'::jsonb,0,'Safety comes first.','original'),
('127.33.d.2.A',2,'In a laboratory investigation, a student should handle chemicals by:','["mixing at random", "reading the label and following directions", "leaving them uncapped", "tasting them"]'::jsonb,1,'Labels give safety information.','original'),
('127.33.d.2.B',3,'Conserving resources during a lab activity means:','["spilling intentionally", "leaving water running", "using only what is needed", "using extra"]'::jsonb,2,'Efficiency prevents waste.','original'),
('127.33.d.2.B',3,'Used chemicals from an experiment should be:','["left on the table", "thrown in a river", "poured in any drain", "disposed of using approved procedures"]'::jsonb,3,'Proper disposal protects people and environment.','original'),
('127.33.d.3.A',2,'Minerals, forests and soil are all:','["natural resources", "tools only", "entertainment", "manufactured goods"]'::jsonb,0,'They occur naturally.','original'),
('127.33.d.3.B',3,'A renewable energy source is one that:','["runs out in a year", "is naturally replenished", "comes only from mines", "can never be used"]'::jsonb,1,'Sun and wind are replenished.','original'),
('127.33.d.3.B',3,'Which energy resource is non-renewable?','["sunlight", "tides", "coal", "wind"]'::jsonb,2,'Coal takes millions of years to form.','original'),
('127.33.d.3.C',3,'A downside of burning fossil fuels for power is:','["more water", "cleaner skies", "richer soil", "air pollution"]'::jsonb,3,'Combustion releases pollutants.','original'),
('127.33.d.3.C',3,'Oil and gas drilling can help the agricultural economy by:','["providing income from leased land", "closing roads", "ending all farming", "lowering all costs"]'::jsonb,0,'Mineral leases pay landowners.','original'),
('127.33.d.3.D',3,'Maps of where resources are used show:','["only prices", "geographic patterns of use", "only weather", "only names"]'::jsonb,1,'Maps display where resources are located and consumed.','original'),
('127.33.d.3.D',3,'Population density affects natural resource use because:','["people need nothing", "density removes demand", "more people usually need more resources", "it has no link"]'::jsonb,2,'Demand rises with people.','original'),
('127.33.d.4.A',3,'A mineral lease agreement lets a company:','["skip paying", "avoid all rules", "own the land forever", "extract minerals from land in exchange for payment"]'::jsonb,3,'Leases grant rights for a fee.','original'),
('127.33.d.4.A',3,'A lease for grazing land would usually state:','["the rent, term and allowed uses", "nothing", "only the weather", "the lessee''s age"]'::jsonb,0,'Leases spell out terms.','original'),
('127.33.d.4.B',3,'A landowner should interpret a legal document by:','["signing without reading", "reading terms carefully and asking for help if unclear", "ignoring clauses", "guessing the meaning"]'::jsonb,1,'Legal documents must be understood.','original'),
('127.33.d.4.B',3,'A royalty in an energy contract is:','["a fine", "a free gift", "a payment based on production", "a tax refund"]'::jsonb,2,'Royalties pay the owner per unit produced.','original'),
('127.33.d.4.C',4,'The public often wants natural resource management to emphasize:','["destroying habitats", "ignoring pollution", "closing parks", "protecting the environment"]'::jsonb,3,'Public interest centers on conservation.','original'),
('127.33.d.4.C',4,'Industry interests in natural resource management usually emphasize:','["access to resources and economic return", "banning production", "eliminating profit", "shutting down business"]'::jsonb,0,'Industry values productive use.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.A',3,'A law affecting natural resource use is:','["a lunch menu", "a land-use regulation", "a sports rule", "a school bell schedule"]'::jsonb,1,'Regulations govern use.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.A',3,'Policy affecting natural resources is usually set by:','["only retailers", "only individuals", "governments and agencies", "only students"]'::jsonb,2,'Agencies create and enforce policy.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.B',3,'Policy affecting energy production covers things such as:','["lunch menus", "parking rules only", "movie ratings", "drilling permits and emissions limits"]'::jsonb,3,'Energy policy sets rules for production.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.B',3,'Subsidies for renewable energy are meant to:','["encourage its development", "raise its cost", "remove it from markets", "stop its use"]'::jsonb,0,'Incentives promote use.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.C',3,'A control that protects natural resources is:','["ignoring violations", "a permit requirement for pollution", "unlimited dumping", "no monitoring"]'::jsonb,1,'Permits limit harm.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.C',3,'Conservation easements protect land by:','["building roads", "removing trees", "limiting future development", "encouraging pollution"]'::jsonb,2,'Easements keep land natural.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.D',3,'A Texas agency that regulates oil and gas is the:','["Parks Department only", "Lottery Commission", "Postal Service", "Railroad Commission"]'::jsonb,3,'The Railroad Commission oversees oil and gas.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.D',3,'A federal agency that manages public lands is the:','["Bureau of Land Management", "Department of Education", "Postal Service", "Federal Reserve"]'::jsonb,0,'BLM oversees public lands.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.E',3,'Property owners play a role in resource development by:','["having no choices", "deciding whether to lease or sell rights", "avoiding all laws", "ignoring neighbors"]'::jsonb,1,'Owners make decisions about their land.','original'),
('127.33.d.5.E',3,'Society''s role in resource development includes:','["staying silent", "avoiding input", "expressing needs through voting and public comment", "removing rules"]'::jsonb,2,'Citizens influence policy.','original'),
('127.33.d.6.A',3,'An advantage of land use planning is:','["random growth", "no rules", "more conflicts", "organized development that protects resources"]'::jsonb,3,'Planning reduces conflicts.','original'),
('127.33.d.6.A',3,'A disadvantage of strict land use planning for some owners is:','["limits on what they can do with their land", "lower taxes", "more freedom", "no restrictions"]'::jsonb,0,'Rules can restrict choices.','original'),
('127.33.d.6.B',4,'A land use trend in many Texas areas is:','["more farms in cities", "conversion of farmland to housing", "no growth", "fewer people"]'::jsonb,1,'Urban growth consumes farmland.','original'),
('127.33.d.6.B',4,'Compared with rural counties, fast-growing metro areas often have:','["fewer people", "less demand", "more land use regulation", "no regulation"]'::jsonb,2,'Growth brings regulation.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.A',3,'An industrial use of water is:','["watering a lawn", "brushing teeth", "bathing", "cooling in a power plant"]'::jsonb,3,'Plants use water for cooling.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.A',3,'Municipal water use refers to water used by:','["cities and towns", "only factories", "only wildlife", "only farms"]'::jsonb,0,'Municipal means city supply.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.B',3,'A way to recycle water is to:','["dump it in lakes", "treat wastewater for reuse", "let it evaporate", "pour it in the street"]'::jsonb,1,'Reuse saves fresh supplies.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.B',3,'Reclaimed water is often used for:','["drinking only", "bottled water", "irrigating golf courses and landscapes", "baby formula"]'::jsonb,2,'Treated water suits irrigation.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.C',3,'A factory pipe discharging into a stream is an example of:','["non-point pollution", "natural flow", "clean runoff", "point source pollution"]'::jsonb,3,'A single pipe is a point source.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.C',3,'Runoff from many city streets carrying oil is:','["non-point source pollution", "point source pollution", "a regulation", "clean water"]'::jsonb,0,'Diffuse runoff is non-point.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.D',3,'A practice to reduce non-point pollution on farms is:','["bare soil", "buffer strips along streams", "dumping waste", "more fertilizer than needed"]'::jsonb,1,'Buffers filter runoff.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.D',3,'Cities abate stormwater pollution by:','["paving more", "removing drains", "building retention ponds", "dumping trash"]'::jsonb,2,'Ponds capture runoff.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.E',3,'When one user withdraws large amounts of water, others may find:','["more water", "water is free", "no change ever", "less water available"]'::jsonb,3,'Supplies are shared.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.E',3,'Drought combined with high demand leads to:','["water shortages", "cheaper water everywhere", "surpluses", "flooding"]'::jsonb,0,'Demand exceeds supply.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.F',3,'Water use legislation helps by:','["ending all use", "setting rules for withdrawals and rights", "creating rain", "removing owners"]'::jsonb,1,'Laws allocate water.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.F',3,'In Texas, groundwater is managed by:','["movie theaters", "post offices", "groundwater conservation districts", "school boards only"]'::jsonb,2,'Districts regulate pumping.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.G',3,'Water quality policy affects farm decisions by:','["ending crops", "raising rainfall", "removing soil", "limiting fertilizer or pesticide runoff"]'::jsonb,3,'Producers must manage inputs.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.G',3,'A producer follows water quality policy when choosing to:','["apply chemicals according to label limits", "skip buffers", "spray before storms", "dump leftover chemicals"]'::jsonb,0,'Labels protect water.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.H',4,'Hydraulic fracturing uses large amounts of:','["paper", "water", "cotton", "wood"]'::jsonb,1,'Energy production needs water.','original'),
('127.33.d.7.H',4,'Power plants need water mainly to:','["water lawns", "fill pools", "produce steam and cool equipment", "wash cars"]'::jsonb,2,'Cooling and steam are major uses.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
